# Clean-room build

BambuFarmer is a first-party **Go** codebase. Grow it with thin interfaces and optional compose services—not by importing another product's tree.

## Do

- Implement features against our own contracts (`packages/farm.ControlPlane`, `packages/api`, Redis Streams, Go migrations).
- Use public product marketing / our FM research docs as **capability** inspiration only.
- Keep the stack Go + Podman-first; one module → one image → one container.

## Do not

- Vendor, mirror, submodule, or paste third-party product **source** into this repository (including "reference", "upstream", or scratch clones under the tree).
- Leave research dumps, extracted trees, or copied AGPL/GPL application code as repo artifacts.
- Migrate the stack to Python/TypeScript or collapse services into an all-in-one image.

Local scratch outside git (and covered by `.gitignore`) is fine; never commit it.
